PART 10 — ADD / UPDATE / REMOVE LOGIC

Implement controlled data lifecycle operations.

ADD

Add when a required record does not exist:

- New Anime streaming record.
- New Season.
- New Episode.
- New Provider.
- New Source.
- First successfully resolved Stream URL.
- Missing discovery information.
- Required count summary.

Prevent duplicate records.

UPDATE

Update when existing data changes:

- Provider status.
- Source status.
- Quality.
- Codec.
- Audio language.
- Stream URL.
- URL expiry.
- Discovery status.
- Provider count.
- Source count.
- Season count.
- Total Episode count.
- Per-season Episode count.
- Version.
- Validation timestamps.

A failed Resolve must never overwrite a working URL.

An Admin refresh must not interrupt active playback.

New versions should be used for future playback and recovery.

REMOVE

Remove only when records are confirmed invalid or permanently obsolete:

- Confirmed duplicate Source.
- Permanently unavailable Provider.
- Permanently removed Source.
- Confirmed obsolete URL.
- Confirmed removed streaming Episode.
- Confirmed removed streaming Season.

Use soft deletion first where practical.

Use a status such as "REMOVED" or a "deleted_at" timestamp.

Do not remove a record because of:

- Timeout.
- Temporary HTTP failure.
- Temporary provider outage.
- Device network interruption.
- One user's playback failure.

Never delete the last known working URL simply because a refresh attempt failed.

A removal event must synchronize to Room so deleted records do not reappear from local cache.

